      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While it sounds good, I don't really necessarily approve of community managed blocklists because if any one person has a vendetta, they can mess over an otherwise fine user: ie if furry A made TDA B mad, furries would be autohidden just out of spite from the TDAs and not any moral objection. I think this should be a personal list thing only. \nHowever, having people block avatars might be a thing to create a better flagging system if several people manually flag an avatar and set it to hidden by creator, those instances of malicious crasher shader users might get addressed faster than they do now. Which certainly feels like never.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
